\title{Post-Quantum Pressure}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Hash-based proof systems are plausibly post-quantum and [pairing-based](dhsorens-0032) ones are not, which turns a cryptographic deadline into an architectural constraint on [wrapping](dhsorens-003P).
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{What is at risk and what is not: discrete-log commitments, hash-based commitments, the ROM analysis in a quantum setting.}
        \li{Hash-based signatures and aggregation, and why a SNARK is the aggregation mechanism.}
        \li{Lattice-based commitments as an alternative, and their cost profile.}
        \li{The consequence for the last step of a pipeline that currently ends in Groth16.}
        \li{What VCV-io's lattice work already covers.}
    }
}
